fail b.cue
exit 1
rerun

A rewrite fails without --force: nothing is written, not even the files
that converted, the version stays, and the report names both ways
forward. Once the failure is gone, a rerun converts everything.

-- cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"

language: version: "v0.17.0"

-- a.cue --
package p

X=a: {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- b.cue --
package p

Y=b: {c: Y.d, d: 1}
-- expect/stderr --
b.cue:1:1: injected rewrite failure
mod upgrade: 1 file(s) could not be converted; nothing written, language version left at v0.17.0
    to convert the other files now and stay at v0.17.0, then fix the files above by hand and run the upgrade again:
        cue fix -f --exp=aliasv2,explicitopen
    to upgrade anyway, leaving those files invalid at v0.18.0:
        cue mod upgrade --force v0.18.0
-- expect2/a.cue --
package p

a~(X): {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- expect2/b.cue --
package p

b~(Y): {c: Y.d, d: 1}
-- expect2/cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"
language: version: "v0.18.0"
